# API container (used with: docker run --env-file deploy/api.env ... comm-center-api)
# On a user-defined Docker network the database host is the db container's name.
# Keep the user, password and database equal to deploy/db.env, and the password URL-safe.
DATABASE_URL=mysql+pymysql://comm_center:change-me-app@cc-db:3306/comm_center
# Signs login tokens. Use a long random value (openssl rand -hex 32).
JWT_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-value
# Derives each Android phone's webhook signing key. Use a long random value (openssl rand -hex 32).
WEBHOOK_SECRET=change-me-to-another-long-random-value
# Push notifications for staff (optional). The API needs only the public key; the private key and
# the subject go to the notifier (deploy/notifier.env). Make the pair with `python -m app.cli vapid-keys`.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# PUSH_AGGREGATE_SECONDS=5
